From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 08:55:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Answer the chunk load queue filter from a hash set

filterChunkLoadQueue snapshots the player's pending chunk queue, then walks the whole
(2 * viewDistance + 1)^2 spiral asking the snapshot whether each coordinate was already
queued. As an ArrayList that was a linear scan per step: at view distance 10, roughly
441 * 441 ChunkCoordIntPair.equals calls every time a player crosses 8 blocks.

The snapshot is only ever probed with contains(), and the order the queue is rebuilt in
comes from the spiral rather than from the snapshot, so a HashSet is an exact substitute.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerChunkMap.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerChunkMap.java
index 80e253b11e85d99ebe20461b747abd61918a72f2..c6976286d2aeb8a9de6cdc23de1f11ab0f3e6264 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerChunkMap.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerChunkMap.java
@@ -190,7 +190,15 @@ public class PlayerChunkMap {
     }
 
     public void filterChunkLoadQueue(EntityPlayer entityplayer) {
-        ArrayList arraylist = Lists.newArrayList(entityplayer.chunkCoordIntPairQueue);
+        // Athena start - the snapshot is only ever probed with contains().
+        //
+        // This method walks the whole (2 * viewDistance + 1)^2 spiral and asked the snapshot
+        // whether each coordinate was already queued. As an ArrayList that was a linear scan per
+        // step, so a view distance of 10 cost ~441 * 441 ChunkCoordIntPair.equals calls every time
+        // a player crossed 8 blocks. Nothing here depends on the snapshot's order - the order the
+        // queue is rebuilt in comes from the spiral below - so a HashSet is an exact substitute.
+        java.util.Set<ChunkCoordIntPair> arraylist = new java.util.HashSet<ChunkCoordIntPair>(entityplayer.chunkCoordIntPairQueue);
+        // Athena end
         int i = 0;
         int j = entityplayer.viewDistance; // PaperSpigot - Player view distance API
         int k = (int) entityplayer.locX >> 4;
